        "Gather the overhanging edges of the cheesecloth together above the yogurt and tie them securely with kitchen twine, creating a bundled pouch. Thread a wooden spoon or chopstick through the tied knot and suspend it over the rim of a tall container such as a large pitcher, tall pot, or deep bowl. The yogurt bundle should hang freely without touching the bottom of the container, allowing gravity to slowly pull the whey downward and out of the yogurt. This suspended method is more effective than simply sitting the strainer in a bowl, because the whey can drip freely from all surfaces rather than pooling at the bottom and slowing the process.",
        "Place the entire setup in the refrigerator. For a spreadable labneh with a consistency similar to cream cheese, strain for 24 hours. For a very thick, dense, moldable labneh that can be rolled into balls, strain for the full 48 hours. Check the container periodically and pour out the collected whey if it rises high enough to touch the bottom of the cheesecloth bundle. Save the whey if you like: it is rich in protein and can be used in smoothies, bread dough, or as a cooking liquid for grains.",
