        "Fry the patties in batches of 4 to 5, being careful not to crowd the pan, which drops the oil temperature and causes the patties to absorb oil and become greasy. Cook for 3 minutes on the first side without moving them, allowing a golden-brown crust to form that will hold the patty together when you flip it. Turn each patty carefully with a thin spatula and cook for 3 minutes on the second side until equally golden and crispy. The patties should feel firm and hold together confidently when lifted.",
        "Remove the cooked patties with a slotted spatula and transfer to a wire rack set over a baking sheet to drain. The wire rack allows air to circulate underneath, keeping the bottom crust crispy. Serve warm with a generous squeeze of fresh lemon juice, which brightens the earthy leek flavor beautifully."
